back in 2016 apple did the unthinkable  they went up on stage and announced the  iphone 7  the first iphone to get rid of the  headphone jack which caused  a lot of people to get upset but apple  had  a solution and that was airpods  which they debuted alongside the iphone  7 and  in just a couple of years they went  absolutely viral  and the rest is history well now in 2021  we're finally expecting the regular  airpods to get its first major redesign  after five years  with the brand new airpods 3 that will  be coming out in just  one month alongside the iphone 13. and  if you don't believe me  i've got a bunch of leaks and rumors to  discuss that will basically confirm the  release of these new airpods so in this  video  i'm going to talk about the airpods 3  and all of the specs and features we're  expecting them to get  and then i'm going to compare them to  the previous airpods 2  the airpods pro and even the future  airpods pro 2  which are expected to come next year but  before i get into all that fun stuff  let's jump into the major leagues rumors  that we have so far about the airpods 3.  in february of 2020 it was reported that  apple was working on airpods pro lite  which basically looked like the pros but  lacked the noise cancellation features  which has now been confirmed to be air  pods 3.  and then in april digitime has basically  reported the same thing  but the new airpods 3 will simply have a  similar design to the pros  adding that they've been delayed into  2021 because of covid and once again in  june we heard the exact same  but this time coming from the reliable  analyst ming chi quo  in october of 2020 mark german from  bloomberg  confirmed airpods 3 are coming with the  pros design and without anc  but also adding that it'll have improved  battery life  and an upgraded wireless chip most  likely being the h2  moving on ming chukwu then claimed that  the airpods 3  will actually have a hybrid design  somewhere between the airpods too  and the airpods pro and then after that  we got our very first  look at a leaked pair of airpods 3 from  52 audio  where they look a lot like the airpod  pros but without the silicon tips  and by the way if you don't know who 52  audio is  that's the website which successfully  leaked the design of the airpods pro  before  they were released so they definitely  have a good track record  and according to the elec the airpods 3  may cost  1.99 which is actually the same price of  the current airpods 2 with their  wireless case  now here's a leak that's pretty insane  mr white shared a photo of an airpods  component  in black now this is something that i  honestly  can't imagine happening and personally  wouldn't really be excited for  because the pure white color of airpods  is extremely iconic  but you guys let me know what you think  after that 52 audio  started releasing more images of the new  air paws 3  and john prosser ended up saying that  those leaks are legitimate  then on march 10th gizmo china released  some brand new renders of the airpods 3  and they look basically identical to the  ones that 52 audio previously showed  we then got even more images of the  airpods 3 from 52 audio  which makes it convincing that these are  the exact air pods we will see at launch  and at the same time 52 audio added that  the price tag  will most likely be around 150 dollars  but i personally think that 200 is more  realistic  and then a few days later an investor's  note from ming chi quo  stated that mass manufacturing of  airpods 3  would begin in quarter 3 of 2021 which  starts  in july which means that airpods 3 are  being made  right now as we speak and very recently  on july 23rd  we got a new leak from deja times saying  that shipments of pcb  and sip modules or basically the chips  have started to take off which pretty  much suggests that we could be getting  air pods  this fall and then right after that we  got a tweet from dylan dkt  an apple analyst and ios developer  confirming that airpods 3 will release  this september  alongside the new iphone which would  line up perfectly to the leak from  digitimes  since then mark grimmon reported the  same thing agreeing with dylan dkt  so it looks like we're going to see  airpods at the same time that the next  iphone comes out  which makes a lot of sense now something  very interesting that has to do with  both airpods 3  and the next iphone is the new possible  support  for wireless lossless audio apple  released  lossless audio for apple music this past  june  for those with ios 14.6 and later  and to listen to it you need to either  use a wired connection  or use the built-in speakers in your  device now the weird part is that apple  is going  all in on lossless audio with them  announcing that they're going to try to  move their entire catalog  over to supporting lossless and the  reason it's weird is because of one  major issue right now you can't stream  lossless audio using wireless devices  like airpods airpods pro and even  airpods max  because current bluetooth connections  don't support lossless  however we've seen a lot of leaks about  the new iphone 13  coming with updated wi-fi 6e and  bluetooth 5.2  as well as mark rimmon saying that the  airpods 3 will have an upgraded wireless  chip  and those upgrades will make it possible  to add support for wireless lossless  audio  and we know that apple's been pushing  lossless like crazy lately  and there is no way that apple will  leave out their airpods from lossless  listening  apple makes a lot of money from airpods  sales  in 2020 airpods made more revenue than  nvidia  and amd combined and almost just as much  as netflix  and guess what apple makes even more  money from  services so it's a no-brainer move to  give airpods support for wireless  lossless  since it'll incentivize a lot of people  to get both new airpods  and an apple music subscription now  there are multiple ways that apple can  actually make this happen  so if you guys are curious let me know  and we might make a dedicated video  going into detail on exactly how apple  can pull this off  now with all that out of the way should  you upgrade to the aeropods 3  well that all depends on what you're  upgrading from  if you currently have airpods pro then  you should absolutely  not to get the airpods 3. as we know the  airpods 3 are going to adopt the pros  design  but they are not going to come with  active noise cancellation so there's  really no point in even  considering it because all you're doing  is downgrading to basically the same  device  but without anc apple is instead  targeting the airpods 3 to people who  still have the first  and second generation airpods from years  ago which is surprisingly  a lot of people even vadim one of the  hosts of this channel  still has the original airpods from  2016.  and for now he says he's totally fine  with them and there are actually many  people that actually prefer the regular  airpods to the airpods pro  because of the open-ear design compared  to an in-ear and i even know an  apple fanboy that loves to drop cash on  the coolest and most expensive products  and even he didn't upgrade to the pros  because he loves the fit of the regular  air paws  that much and as i said before the  airpods 3 are set to release at a price  of around 150 to 200  i'm honestly expecting the latter which  honestly is really good considering that  the airpods 2 with the wireless case  have an msrp of that much so if you have  air pods it's definitely worth upgrading  if you're considering it  now if you currently have airpods pro  and want to upgrade the only worthwhile  option  is to wait for the airpods pro 2. so  let's talk about what those are going to  be like  in october of 2020 mark grumman claimed  that the new airpods pro 2  will come with a brand new circular  design and an upgraded wireless chip  this definitely makes sense because if  the new airpods 3 are adopting the  airpod pro's current design  then they need to update the design of  the pros too so that they'll stand out  and there are already a lot of earbuds  out there like the amazon echo buds and  the galaxy buds that have a stainless  circular design  and they are fantastic having a flush  design makes earbuds much more  comfortable to lay down with  and you're easily able to do things like  change your shirt or a helmet  and not only that but they'd allow for  bigger batteries as well as far as the  release  ming chi kuo says not to expect the  airpods pro 2  until 2022 so it'll be a wait but there  have been a lot of whispers about a new  innovative experience that could have to  do with health tracking  and interestingly digitimes actually  reported that apple was gonna pack  ambient light sensors into a set of  airpods in the future  and apple track's take on their rumor  was that apple would use those sensors  to measure your heart rate and other  biometrics  as it would possibly be more accurate  than measuring on your wrist with an  apple watch  so that could be one of the added  exclusives to make the pro 2 stand out  even more  so based on those leaks if you currently  have the airpods pro  then you should sit with them for the  time being until the pro 2 get released  and if you have the gen 1 or gen 2 air  pods  then the upcoming redesign with the new  wireless chip is  definitely worth getting these new  airpods are going to be game changers  especially being the first wireless  apple products that could support  lossless audio  if you guys want to see a dedicated  video on how apple can pull that off  then click the subscribe button above  and hit the bell to be notified  so you don't miss out check out those  two videos over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one
 

